            "annotations": [],
            "text": "{\"description\":\"The first photograph shows a tall carved stone surface with shallow relief figures, including three arch-topped shapes along the upper band and several animal-like forms below. In the middle and lower areas there are birdlike heads with curved beaks, a small circular disk-like carving, and other worn linear incisions. Some edges and details are obscured by erosion, shadow, and adjacent stones.\",\"avian\":{\"answer\":\"present\",\"evidence\":\"Several carved figures have birdlike heads or hooked beaks, especially the large lower-left figure with a clear curved beak and eye on the visible stone surface.\",\"box\":[0.18,0.72,0.36,0.97]},\"large_face\":{\"answer\":\"absent\",\"evidence\":\"No large human face with facial features is visible on the main surface; the visible figures are animal-like or abstract rather than a large human face.\",\"box\":null},\"scorpion\":{\"answer\":\"uncertain\",\"evidence\":\"There are curved and segmented-looking incisions among the animal figures, but no clearly readable scorpion with both legs and/or an upturned segmented tail can be identified reliably.\",\"box\":null},\"round_motif\":{\"answer\":\"present\",\"evidence\":\"A distinct small round carved disk appears near the center of the upper main panel, separate from eyes or nostrils.\",\"box\":[0.35,0.39,0.44,0.48]},\"three_arches\":{\"answer\":\"present\",\"evidence\":\"Three repeated arch-topped forms are arranged side by side across the top band of the carved surface.\",\"box\":[0.05,0.02,0.79,0.25]},\"limitations\":\"The relief is weathered and unevenly lit, with strong shadows, worn lines, and some obstruction by adjacent stones near the lower left, making fine details difficult to read.\"}",
